<section class="sec t-light h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:15;--mrows:27">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/5/12;--m:8/2/11/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3 class="ta-center">Marriage Counseling in Orem</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/15/14/26;--m:1/2/8/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/marriage-therapy-867cc8.jpg" alt="A marriage therapist at Tangible Therapy in Orem, Utah sits across from a couple in a warmly lit office" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/2/15/14;--m:11/2/27/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>A lot of couples wait until things feel broken before they call. You don’t have to. Our Orem marriage counselors help couples rebuild communication, work through conflict and trust issues, navigate parenting and in-law stress, and reconnect when the relationship has started to feel like a logistics arrangement. Several of our therapists are trained in the Gottman Method, one of the most researched approaches to couples work, which means you leave sessions with practical tools you can actually use in your next hard conversation, not just a place to vent.</p><p>Couples counseling at our Orem office is available weekdays and evenings, and many insurance plans cover it. Not sure if therapy is what your marriage needs? Book a free 15-minute consult with one of our couples therapists and ask them directly.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:17;--mrows:19">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/2/16/13;--m:1/2/8/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/teen-2d0f45.jpg" alt="A Teen Counselor at Tangible Therapy in Orem sits across from a teen client" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/15/5/25;--m:8/2/10/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>Therapy for Teens in Orem</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/14/16/26;--m:10/2/18/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>If you’re a parent watching your teenager struggle; anxiety, slipping grades, a shrinking social circle, anger that came out of nowhere, or a kid who used to talk to you and doesn’t anymore- you’re probably wondering whether it’s "just a phase" or time to get help. Here’s a simple rule: if it’s been weeks and it’s affecting school, sleep, friendships, or your family, it’s worth a conversation with a counselor.</p><p>Our Orem teen therapists are good at the hardest part: getting a teenager to actually engage. Sessions don’t feel like a lecture or an interrogation; therapists meet teens where they are, and because Tangible is skills-based, your teen leaves with practical tools for managing anxiety, big emotions, social stress, and self-esteem, not just an hour of talking. We work with teens on anxiety and depression, school and social pressure, identity questions, ADHD, and family conflict.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-light h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:38;--mrows:60">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/7/13;--m:1/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2>Why Orem Clients Choose Tangible Therapy</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/15/16/26;--m:34/2/41/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/chatgpt-image-may-13-2026-07-59-32-pm-671428.jpg" alt="" width="1402" height="1122" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:7/2/9/13;--m:5/2/8/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>There's no shortage of therapists in Utah County. Here's what makes Tangible Therapy different:</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:9/2/11/12;--m:8/2/10/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><h3>Training that goes further</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:11/2/15/12;--m:10/2/16/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="rte"><p>Every Tangible therapist completes twice the industry-standard training hours — all at certification level. That means you're working with someone who has genuinely mastered their approach, not just completed a weekend workshop. All of our therapists are EMDR trained. </p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:16/2/27/13;--m:16/2/23/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/chatgpt-image-may-13-2026-07-50-50-pm-124b1a.jpg" alt="" width="1402" height="1122" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:18/15/21/25;--m:24/2/27/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="rte"><h3>Affordable care — with or without insurance</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:21/15/26/25;--m:27/2/33/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><div class="rte"><p>We accept most major insurance plans, including Select Health, PEHP, BlueCross BlueShield, Aetna, DMBA, and United Healthcare. The average Tangible client pays just $25 per session after insurance. For clients without coverage, our cash pay rate is $115 per session — one of the lowest rates in Utah Valley for this level of training and expertise.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:27/15/39/25;--m:51/2/61/10;--dz:7;--mz:7"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px;--fit:contain"><img src="/images/best-of-state-37052a.jpg" alt="An image depicting Tangible Therapy&#x27;s Best of state award, their best of utah County award and their top-rated google reviews in utah symbol." width="1051" height="872" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:29/2/32/12;--m:41/2/44/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><div class="rte"><h3>A practice that's earned your trust</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:32/2/36/12;--m:44/2/51/10;--dz:6;--mz:6"><div class="rte"><p>We've been named Best Counseling Center of Utah Valley two years in a row and Best of State Utah in 2026. We're consistently top-rated on Google across Utah. Those recognitions matter to us, but what matters more is that our clients actually feel better — and come back to tell us so.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

