  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">✺ Frequently asked questions ✺</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/16/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>How do I get started at the Orem office?</summary><div class="rte"><p>The easiest way is to call us at 435-260-5406 or book through our client portal. We offer a free 15-minute phone consultation so you can connect with a therapist before committing to a full session. Most new clients are seen within 1–2 weeks.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you accept my insurance at the Orem location?</summary><div class="rte"><p>We accept most major insurance plans including Select Health, PEHP, BlueCross BlueShield, Aetna, DMBA, United Healthcare, Tricare, EMI Health and more. Call us or visit our insurance page and we'll verify your benefits for free before your first appointment.</p></div></details><details><summary>How much does therapy cost at the Orem office?</summary><div class="rte"><p>If you have insurance, the average Tangible Therapy client pays around $25 per session after their benefits are applied. Our cash pay rate for clients without insurance is $115 per session — one of the most affordable rates in Utah Valley for this quality of care.</p></div></details><details><summary>How soon can I get an appointment?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Most new clients are scheduled within 1–2 weeks. If you have a specific therapist or specialization in mind, availability varies — but we'll do our best to match you quickly. Call 435-260-5406 or book online to get started.</p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/14/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Where exactly is the Orem office located?</summary><div class="rte"><p>We're at 246 N Orem Blvd, Orem, UT 84057 — just off State Street with free parking available out front. There's no receptionist on-site, but our off-site team is available by phone if you have any questions when you arrive. Your therapist will come get you from the waiting room when they're ready.</p></div></details><details><summary>What therapy approaches do your Orem therapists use?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Our Orem team is trained in EMDR, Gottman Method couples therapy, IFS (Internal Family Systems), Brainspotting, CBT (Cognitive Behavioral Therapy), and somatic approaches. All therapists complete twice the industry-standard training at certification level — so whatever you're working through, we have someone qualified to help.</p><p><br/></p></div></details><details><summary>Can I switch to telehealth if I can&#x27;t come in?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Absolutely. All of our services are available via telehealth for clients anywhere in Utah. If you start in-person and need to switch, or want to mix in-person and online sessions, we can accommodate that with the same therapist.</p></div></details></div></div>
